This file exists so that `tally_connector/public/` is present in a fresh clone.

frappe/build.py only creates the /assets/<app> symlink for an app whose public
directory already exists at the moment `bench build` runs:

    if os.path.isdir(app_assets):
        symlinks[app_assets] = os.path.join(assets_path, app_name)

Everything under public/ here is Vite output and is gitignored, so without this
file the directory does not exist in a clone. If a deployment runs `bench build`
before the frontend build has produced public/frontend - which is what Frappe
Cloud does - no symlink is ever created, every /assets/tally_connector/... URL
404s, and the dashboard renders as a blank page with no error on the server side.

The CRM and Helpdesk apps carry the same file for the same reason; Helpdesk
carries nothing else under public/ at all.
